@attribute [Route(pageUrl)]
@attribute [Route(pageUrl2)]
@layout DocsMainLayout

<PageMetaTags PageUrl="@pageUrl" Title="@metaTitle" Description="@metaDescription" ImageUrl="@imageUrl" />

<PageHero Title="@pageTitle">
    <SubTitleTemplate>
        @((MarkupString)pageDescription)
    </SubTitleTemplate>
</PageHero>

<section class="be-release-spotlight">
    <p class="be-release-kicker">New in 2.0.0</p>
    <h2 class="be-release-title">Time axes, JavaScript functions, chart methods and events</h2>
    <p class="be-release-copy">
        2.0.0 also covers far more Chart.js 4.6 options. It changes some defaults, so if you are upgrading from 1.x, read the breaking changes first.
    </p>
    <div class="buttons mt-3 mb-0">
        <a class="button is-primary is-small" href="@DemoRouteConstants.Blog_Release_2_0_0">Read the 2.0.0 release notes</a>
        <a class="button is-small" href="@(DemoRouteConstants.Blog_Release_2_0_0)#breaking-changes">Breaking changes</a>
    </div>
</section>

<div class="content">
    <Section Class="p-0" Size="HeadingSize.H4" Name="Introduction" PageUrl="@pageUrl" Link="introduction">
        <Block>
            <p>
                BlazorExpress.ChartJS is an open-source Blazor component library for <a href="https://www.chartjs.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Chart.js</a>.
                You describe a chart's data and options in C#; the library draws it with Chart.js in the browser, and updates, resizes and disposes it with the component.
                It runs in Blazor WebAssembly, Blazor Web Apps (Server and Auto render modes) and .NET MAUI Blazor Hybrid apps, on .NET 8, 9 and 10, under the Apache-2.0 license.
            </p>
        </Block>
    </Section>
</div>

<div class="be-intro-grid mb-5">
    <div class="be-intro-card">
        <p class="be-intro-card-title">Eight chart types</p>
        <p>Bar, bubble, doughnut, line, pie, polar area, radar and scatter, each a Razor component.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="be-intro-card">
        <p class="be-intro-card-title">Typed options</p>
        <p>Chart.js data, datasets, options and plugins as C# classes, with IntelliSense and XML docs.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="be-intro-card">
        <p class="be-intro-card-title">Time axes</p>
        <p>Date labels and points from <code>DateOnly</code>, <code>DateTime</code> or <code>DateTimeOffset</code>, with no date-adapter script.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="be-intro-card">
        <p class="be-intro-card-title">JavaScript functions</p>
        <p>Register a function once, then use it from C# for tick labels, tooltips, colours and more.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="be-intro-card">
        <p class="be-intro-card-title">Methods and events</p>
        <p>Update, reset, show or hide data, export an image, and handle clicks, legend clicks and hovers in C#.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="be-intro-card">
        <p class="be-intro-card-title">@SampleCatalog.All.Count samples</p>
        <p>Copyable samples based on the official Chart.js samples, each with "How to use" steps.</p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="be-intro-links mb-5" aria-label="Chart documentation">
    <a class="tag is-link is-light is-medium" href="@DemoRouteConstants.Docs_BarChart">Bar chart</a>
    <a class="tag is-link is-light is-medium" href="@DemoRouteConstants.Docs_BubbleChart">Bubble chart</a>
    <a class="tag is-link is-light is-medium" href="@DemoRouteConstants.Docs_DoughnutChart">Doughnut chart</a>
    <a class="tag is-link is-light is-medium" href="@DemoRouteConstants.Docs_LineChart">Line chart</a>
    <a class="tag is-link is-light is-medium" href="@DemoRouteConstants.Docs_PieChart">Pie chart</a>
    <a class="tag is-link is-light is-medium" href="@DemoRouteConstants.Docs_PolarAreaChart">Polar area chart</a>
    <a class="tag is-link is-light is-medium" href="@DemoRouteConstants.Docs_RadarChart">Radar chart</a>
    <a class="tag is-link is-light is-medium" href="@DemoRouteConstants.Docs_ScatterChart">Scatter chart</a>
</div>

<div class="content">
    <Section Class="p-0" Size="HeadingSize.H4" Name="Quick start" PageUrl="@pageUrl" Link="quick-start">
        <Block>
            <p>
                Four steps add a first chart to an existing Blazor project. For a full walkthrough for your project type, see the
                <a href="@(pageUrl)#setup-guides">setup guides</a>.
            </p>
            <ol>
                <li>
                    <b>Install the package</b> with the .NET CLI:
                    <CodeChunk Class="mt-3" LanguageCode="LanguageCode.Text" FilePath="~\Pages\Docs\GettingStarted\net8\01_A_Manual_Install_01_Run_Net_CLI_Command_Snippet.razor" ProjectRootClassType="DemoAppConstants.ProjectRootClassType" />
                    or add a package reference to your project file:
                    <CodeChunk Class="mt-3" LanguageCode="LanguageCode.Text" FilePath="~\Pages\Docs\GettingStarted\net8\01_A_Manual_Install_02_Add_Package_Reference_Snippet.razor" ProjectRootClassType="DemoAppConstants.ProjectRootClassType" />
                </li>
                <li>
                    <b>Add the scripts</b> at the end of the <code>body</code>, in this order: Chart.js, the data labels plugin (only if you use data labels), then <code>blazorexpress.chartjs.js</code>.
                    Put them in <code>wwwroot/index.html</code> after <code>_framework/blazor.webassembly.js</code> for Blazor WebAssembly,
                    or in <code>Components/App.razor</code> after <code>_framework/blazor.web.js</code> for a Blazor Web App.
                    <CodeChunk Class="mt-3" LanguageCode="LanguageCode.HTML" FilePath="~\Pages\Docs\GettingStarted\net8\01_A_Manual_Install_03_Snippet.html" ProjectRootClassType="DemoAppConstants.ProjectRootClassType" />
                </li>
                <li>
                    <b>Import the namespace</b> in <code>_Imports.razor</code>:
                    <CodeChunk Class="mt-3" LanguageCode="LanguageCode.Razor" FilePath="~\Pages\Docs\GettingStarted\net8\01_A_Manual_Install_04_Snippet.razor" ProjectRootClassType="DemoAppConstants.ProjectRootClassType" />
                </li>
                <li>
                    <b>Add a chart</b> to a page. Chart.js needs the canvas, so the chart is drawn in <code>OnAfterRenderAsync</code> with <code>InitializeAsync</code>.
                    In a Blazor Web App the page must use an interactive render mode.
                    <CodeChunk Class="mt-3" LanguageCode="LanguageCode.Razor" FilePath="~\Pages\Docs\GettingStarted\net8\01_A_Manual_Install_06_Snippet.razor" ProjectRootClassType="DemoAppConstants.ProjectRootClassType" />
                </li>
            </ol>
            <p>
                Next, browse the <a href="@DemoRouteConstants.Demos_Samples">samples gallery</a> or open the docs for your chart type above.
                Each chart's docs page lists its parameters, events and methods.
            </p>
        </Block>
    </Section>

